## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical resilience planning, cross-region deployment, and IaC-driven CI/CD integration with chaos engineering signals.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-region ECS/Fargate with per-branch preview environments
- App Mesh traffic routing for sophisticated traffic management
- Route 53 latency-based routing for optimal user experience
- AWS Fault Injection Simulator as a quality gate before production promotion
- Automatic rollback criteria tied to SLO violations
- DR runbook for regional failover procedures
- Observability-driven development with p95 latency and error rate SLOs

## Code Example
```javascript
// CDK snippet for FIS experiment template (illustrative)
const fisExperiment = new CfnResource(this, 'FISExperiment', {
  type: 'AWS::FIS::ExperimentTemplate',
  properties: {
    description: 'Chaos experiment for p95 latency validation',
    targets: {
      ECSClusterTarget: {
        resourceType: 'AWS::ECS::Cluster',
        selectionMode: 'ALL',
      },
    },
    actions: {
      latencyInjection: {
        actionId: 'aws:chaos:inject:network:latency',
        parameters: {
          duration: 'PT2M',
          latencyMs: '500',
          percentage: '25',
        },
      },
    },
    stopConditions: [{
      source: 'aws:cloudwatch:metric',
      value: 'p95_latency > 200',
    }],
  },
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
This scenario stresses cross-region serverless deployment, traffic routing, and robust DR with fast rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Lambda versions and weighted aliases for canary promotion
- DynamoDB Global Tables for cross-region data consistency
- Route 53 latency routing and automated rollback criteria
- AppConfig feature flags; GitHub Actions/CDK provisioning

## Code Example
```javascript
// CDK sketch for weighted Lambda alias (conceptual)
const fn = new lambda.Function(this, 'Ingest', { runtime: lambda.Runtime.NODEJS_18_X, code: lambda.Code.fromAsset('lambda'), handler: 'index.handler' });
const v1 = fn.currentVersion;
const v2 = new lambda.Version(this, 'IngestV2', { lambda: fn, codeHash: 'abcdef', description: 'v2' });
const prodAlias = new lambda.Alias(this, 'Prod', {
  aliasName: 'prod',
  version: v1,
  additionalVersionWeights: { [v2.versionHash || v2.node.id]: 0.2 }
});
```

